'''''[[Strictly Come Dancing]]''''' aired its '''first series''' on [[BBC One]] from 15 May 2004 to 3 July 2004. The series was presented by [[Bruce Forsyth]] and [[Tess Daly]], while [[Justin Lee Collins]] presented [[BBC Three]]'s spin-off show ''Strictly Come Dancing: On Three''. The judging panel consisted of [[Len Goodman]], [[Arlene Phillips]], [[Craig Revel Horwood]], and [[Bruno Tonioli]].<ref>{{cite news|last=Grieveson-Smith|first=Jess|title=Who were the first celebrities on Strictly Come Dancing and where are they now?|url=https://www.examinerlive.co.uk/news/tv/who-were-first-celebrities-strictly-21862398|work=YorkshireLive|date=16 October 2021|access-date=21 January 2024}}</ref>

On 3 July 2004, journalist [[Natasha Kaplinsky]] and [[Brendan Cole]] were announced as the winners, while ''[[EastEnders]]'' actor [[Christopher Parker]] and [[Hanna Karttunen]] finished in second place.<ref>{{cite news|title=Kaplinsky wins TV dancing contest|url=https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/entertainment/3864373.stm|publisher=[[BBC News]]|date=4 July 2004|access-date=21 January 2024}}</ref>

This was the only series to air in the spring/summer season; all other series of ''Strictly Come Dancing'' would air in the autumn/winter season.

